# The WAL admits a re-presented generation claim against the initiator's entry
# alone, ignoring its routing floor (#5697 review, S1). A cross-shard straddler:
# shard root s2 of the purged incarnation admitted a write whose keys, under the
# re-created tree's shard map, belong to L. L's first initialisation claims only
# its own shard root's generation, not s2's, and s2's re-created counterpart has
# not initialised. With s2's entry retired, only the WAL-side floor refuses the
# claim the write's leaf re-presents; without it, the write is allocated above L's
# recorded close. Moved from the design's ReadPositionHonestRoutingWalIgnoresFloor.
MODULE: StraddlerBelowInitRoutingWalIgnoresFloor
TARGET: StraddlerBelowInit
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the WAL admits a re-presented routing generation at or below the initiator floor
PERTURBS: Represent

--- FIND
    /\ loaded[i] = Unloaded
    /\ pstamp[i] > walFloor[i]
    /\ pstamp[i] >= entryRow[i]
--- REPLACE
    /\ loaded[i] = Unloaded
\* MUTATION: no WAL-side floor check at the claim.
    /\ pstamp[i] >= entryRow[i]
--- END
